{
	title: 'Hal warns and pauses when disk or memory runs low',
	spec: 'The host checks free disk space in the home (statfs bavail × bsize) and available memory (/proc/meminfo MemAvailable on Linux; on macOS total memory × kern.memorystatus_level percent, the figure memory_pressure reports; os.freemem elsewhere; /mem shows the same figure) at start and every 30 s, and grades them: critical under 1 GB of disk or 0.5 GB of memory, low under 5 GB or 1.5 GB, else ok. Thresholds and interval are plain values on the resources object, overridable from local.ts or plugins. Entering a worse level sends every client a warning event naming what is short, how much is left and the limit; clients joining while it lasts get it too; returning to ok sends one recovery warning. While critical, every running turn is paused with that reason (turns.stop), including turns started after the level became critical; this kills their commands and the user resumes. Models hear nothing else about resources: the user is told and fixes the cause. A failed check reaches clients as a warning with the full error. State is in memory; checks never send a message or start a turn. Module: src/host/resources.ts, started by main.becomeHost.',
	status: 'done',
	notes: [
		'Warnings reuse the existing warning event (st.notice in both clients) and host.warn for joining clients, so the web and the terminal show them the same way with no new UI. Notes go into bash results only: bash is what fills disks, and the note then sits in history like neighbor notes, so replay and the cache see the same bytes. A test injects samples into resources.check; the pause path is turns.stop, tested with turns.',
		'Bug fixed: on macOS os.freemem counts only idle pages, not reclaimable cache, so a healthy 16 GB Mac read 0.1 GB and paused every turn as critical. Invariant: available memory means memory the OS can hand out without swapping on every platform.',
		'Resource levels are not model notices: the model cannot free disk or memory, and the pause reason already tells a paused turn. The recovery warning stays because client warnings stay shown until replaced; without it a critical warning would remain after recovery.',
		"Resource warnings use warnings.set('resources', text) in src/host/warnings.ts, so clients joining while short get them. A drop from critical to low now also warns, with the current text. Bug fixed: resources wrapped host.warn at run time; Hal's modules never wrap each other's functions (tasks/README.md)."
	],
	needs: ['0f', 'j1']
}
